  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 331 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nAs the disturbance exits southeast, rain chances then diminish \nthrough the weekend and southerly low level winds advect in warmer\ntemperatures. Near record temperatures are possible Saturday as\nmost locations exceed 100 degrees. Upper level high pressure then\nbecomes established to our east advecting in cooler gulf moisture\nto West Texas and eastern New Mexico. Temperatures ease back from\nthe 100s on Saturday to the upper 90s early next week which is\nstill 5 to 10 degrees above normal for this time of year. The gulf\nair may contain enough moisture to allow for scattered afternoon\nshowers and storms in the higher elevations and adjacent plains\nwest of the Pecos River.\n\nHennig",
